# Canonical Epistack documents

The competition materials under `docs/competition/` are **canonical constraints**
for this repo. Policy: [`docs/competition/CANONICAL.md`](docs/competition/CANONICAL.md).

Canonical set (read when planning or reviewing work that might conflict):

- `docs/competition/epistack.md` — stack vision / objectivity–subjectivity split
- `docs/competition/epistack-competition.md` — brief, layers, case studies, entry shapes
- `docs/competition/judging-criteria.md` — uplift, generalizability, compounding, scalability, transparency, adversarial robustness, insight
- `docs/competition/format-and-length.md` — judge attention budget / format

Prefer live FLF pages if mirrors diverge: https://flf.org/epistack/ and
https://flf.org/epistack-competition/ (PDFs for judging/format appendices).

## Required behavior

When the user’s proposal, plan, or requested change **seems to contravene**
these documents:

1. **Warn before proceeding** — brief, specific: which doc, what tension.
2. **Do not silently implement** the conflicting direction; ask whether to
   proceed as an explicit exception or adjust to fit.
3. Treat “contravene” as material conflict with goals or constraints (not mere
   stylistic preference), e.g.:
   - single-user / non-compounding artifacts as the end product
   - opaque methodology or polished demo without a clear, critiqueable workflow
   - collapsing provenance/structure into uncheckable narrative conclusions
   - one-case overfitting with no generalizability story
   - ignoring the ~10-page core reading budget without a designated entry slice
   - positioning the system as truth-arbiter rather than investigation support

Compatible exploration and tradeoffs are fine; undocumented overrides are not.
